  <div class="post-content"><p>Owning a business in Las Vegas is a huge opportunity — but it also comes with financial responsibilities that many business owners ignore until the IRS comes knocking. Accounting services aren't a luxury. They're the foundation that keeps your business healthy, legal, and ready to grow. In this guide, we'll explain exactly which accounting services your business needs and why you can't operate without them.</p><h2>Monthly bookkeeping</h2><p>Bookkeeping is the organized record of all your business's financial activity: income, expenses, invoices, and payments. Without it, you don't really know whether your business is making or losing money. An accountant keeps this record month by month so you always have complete clarity on your finances.</p><h2>Business tax filing</h2><p>Every business in the US — LLC, S-Corp, or Corporation — is required to file taxes with the IRS every year. Filing incorrectly or late triggers automatic penalties that can add up quickly. An accountant who specializes in business taxes knows exactly which deductions apply to your business and how to legally reduce what you pay.</p><h2>Payroll</h2><p>If you have employees, payroll is one of the most delicate processes in your business. It involves calculating wages, withholding taxes correctly, and making payments to the IRS on time. A payroll mistake can result in serious penalties. A professional payroll service handles all of this for you automatically.</p><h2>Monthly financial reports</h2><p>Your business needs clear reports every month: profit and loss statement, balance sheet, and cash flow. Without these numbers, you can't make smart decisions about growing, hiring, or investing.</p><h2>Tax planning</h2><p>The best accountants don't just file taxes — they also plan ahead to reduce your tax burden for the following year. Tax planning can save you thousands of dollars when done correctly.</p><h2>Representation before the IRS</h2><p>If the IRS sends a letter, opens an audit, or there's an outstanding debt, you need an accountant who can represent you and negotiate on your behalf. Responding on your own can make the situation worse.</p><h2>What happens if you don't have these services?</h2><p>Without professional accounting services, your business is exposed to IRS penalties, incorrect filings, uncontrolled cash flow, and financial decisions based on wrong numbers. Most businesses that close within their first 3 years don't fail from lack of customers — they fail from financial disorder.</p><h2>At Guzman Tax Accounting, we handle it all</h2><p>At Guzman Tax Accounting, we offer complete accounting services for businesses in Las Vegas — bookkeeping, taxes, payroll, and representation before the IRS. All in Spanish, with clear pricing and no hidden fees. Call us at (725) 340-6758 or reach out on WhatsApp.</p><a href="/en/consultation" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top:8px;">Get a Consultation</a></div>
